WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.067
Hello.

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.535
I'm Dana Bash in Washington,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.770
where the state of our union

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.973
is bracing ourselves for a seismic event

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:08.341
as the first ever

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.909
former US president to face

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.344
criminal charges prepares

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.779
to appear in court.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.114
Prosecutors, police,

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:14.981
a Secret Service

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:15.882
and Trump's team

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.083
are working out details

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:17.884
for his arraignment

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:18.985
before a judge

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.321
in a Manhattan criminal court on Tuesday,

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.023
where Donald Trump will face

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.858
a more than 30 count indictment

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.526
related to business fraud.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.661
That indictment is still under seal.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.397
It follows District Attorney

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.197
Alvin Bragg's

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.033
investigation into a hush money

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.567
payment by Trump's

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.902
then personal attorney,

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.636
Michael Cohen,

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.570
to an adult

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.571
film actress

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.774
just before the 2016 election.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.842
In response to form,

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.309
the former

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.944
president is going on the attack,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.846
calling the indictment political,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.181
calling it a persecution

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:51.518
and using it to bolster his own 2024

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.386
presidential campaign.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.287
Well, here with me

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.156
now is the president's former

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.024
president's lawyer for this case.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:58.892
Joe Tacopina,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.160
thank you so much for joining me

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:00.660
this morning.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.062
I first want to ask you

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.763
about what you know

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.465
at this moment about the arraignment,

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.399
how it's going to go.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.201
Walk us through

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.636
what is going to happen

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.638
when the former president shows

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.338
up in New York

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.843
Well, then, I mean, in theory,

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.511
it should be like

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.712
the hundreds of other arraignments

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.780
I've done in that building

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.381
over the

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.182
course of my career,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.951
which is you walk in, you see a judge

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.386
you plead not guilty.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.955
You set a schedule and you leave.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.691
Obviously, this is different.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.326
This has never happened before.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:33.827
I've never had

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.628
Secret Service involved in an arraignment

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.896
before at 100 Center Street.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.132
So the answer to that question

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:39.833
then is

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.067
I honestly don't know how

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:41.668
this is going to go,

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.503
hopefully as smoothly as possible.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.338
And then we begin the

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.906
the battle to right this wrong,

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:47.574
because it's a

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.275
it's a really it's a day that,

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:49.876
in my opinion,

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.111
the rule of law in the United States

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:51.544
has died.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.946
We're going to get to that in a second.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.248
But just on the on the logistics,

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.416
do you know what time it starts

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.354
You know, nothing's been nailed down.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.989
I think that's going to happen tomorrow.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.458
But I think sometime in the afternoon,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.093
will there be a perp walk?

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:07.794
You said you've done

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.761
many of these before.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.865
Most of them do have perp walks

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.233
Not really.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.701
Not in a case like this.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.402
But, you know, look, I anticipate them

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.670
trying to get every ounce

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.272
of publicity out of this

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.474
that they think that they can get.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:21.808
You know,

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.342
I don't know

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.443
if that's going to happen again.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.612
Secret services involved.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:28.748
So hopefully this will be is painless

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.283
and classy as possible

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.284
for a situation like this,

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.652
which I don't even

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.020
know really what brings us here.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.188
But such a different story.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:38.091
Some of the basics are, as you said,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:39.959
you know,

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.395
necessary as part of this process.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.096
Mug shot.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.498
Will we will he have to take a mug shot?

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:48.768
Again?

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:49.536
Danny, your

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.504
question is that I just it's not normal

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.305
operating procedure.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.239
Yeah, it's all up in the air.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:53.840
All the

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:54.841
all the Tuesday stuff

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.242
is still very much up in the air

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.111
on the fact that we will very

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.646
loudly and proudly say not guilty.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.081
Well, you're a very seasoned attorney,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.483
so presumably

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.618
your strategy is not up in the air.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.386
So let's talk

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.087
about what you're thinking about

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.722
when it comes to the legal strategy.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.691
Once Donald Trump is arraigned,

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.592
are you going to move

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.027
to dismiss the case

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.329
right off the bat in the arraignment

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:19.832
and if so, on what grounds?

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.135
No, not we're not doing anything

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:22.735
at the arraignment

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.304
because that would be showmanship

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.038
and nothing more

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.072
because we haven't even seen

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.473
the indictment yet.

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.175
You know, we will take the indictment.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.677
We will dissect it.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.545
The team will look at every every

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.915
potential issue that we will

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:36.783
be able to challenge

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.350
and we will challenge.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:37.817
And, of course,

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.719
I very much anticipated motion

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.386
to dismiss coming,

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.255
because there's no law that fits this.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.756
And you have a situation where,

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.891
you know, the federal government,

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:45.825
the Department of Justice,

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.660
turn this matter down.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.396
The FEC, which governs federal election

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.765
laws, said there's no violation here

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.067
yet somehow

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.302
a state prosecutor has taken a

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.203
a misdemeanor

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.404
and try to cobble together

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.672
to make it a felony

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.840
by alleging a violation

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.277
of federal federal campaign violations.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.212
And the FEC said that doesn't exist.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:06.613
Right.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.814
Well, let me ask you about that,

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:08.748
because you mentioned it.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.882
You've been talking a lot

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:13.219
about the FEC and federal

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.421
investigations and allegations

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:16.689
investigation,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.657
I should say, that

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.092
didn't end up in an indictment

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.326
on the federal level.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.162
But we haven't seen the specifics.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.097
And we should say that over

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:24.664
and over again.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.032
This is still under seal,

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.134
this indictment. But because it is

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:31.704
on a local level, on a state level,

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.607
presumably this will be focused on

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.743
those issues where he allegedly broke

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:37.644
the law there,

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.078
whether it becomes

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:39.646
an issue

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.581
of trying to defraud a business

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:44.017
or something along those lines,

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:46.452
not necessarily

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.288
at the FEC and things that are discussed

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.590
No, no, no, no, no. It can't be.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.925
This was a federal presidential election.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.928
The allegation here in some

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:56.529
twilight zone

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.263
sort of scenario

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:59.432
is that he settled the civil case

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:00.466
six years earlier,

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.801
something that happens, by the way,

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.002
all the time.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.003
A civil case was settled

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.238
with confidentiality agreements

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.173
between a lawyer that was representing

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:07.774
him and a lawyer

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:09.275
representing the Stormy Daniels.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.777
They trusted him to sign

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:11.544
that settlement agreement.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.212
So they signed it.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.580
The lawyer financed it,

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.683
subsequently gave him a host of invoices

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.084
for legal services over the course of

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:18.384
a year.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.286
They were recorded.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:20.987
But understand

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.922
here's the key distinction, Donna.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.458
They were recorded in their entries.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.727
They were never filed anywhere.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.929
They were never filed with the IRS.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.130
They never took the tax deduction

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.665
and they never filed with the FEC

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.100
because they weren't required to.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.002
This was a personal expenditure,

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.470
not a campaign expenditure.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.172
Had it been a campaign expenditure,

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.907
he would have used campaign funds.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:41.574
And then, of course,

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.509
we'd be talking about here today

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.944
the outrage at Donald Trump,

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:45.778
whose campaign funds

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.313
for personal expenditure

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.082
they'd be baying for his scalp.

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:51.117
It's a completely upside down world.

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:52.251
So he's damned if he didn't

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.186
and if he didn't.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.687
So those are misdemeanors.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:55.621
By the way,

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.490
the record entries, which don't exist

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.391
and not for centuries,

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.325
but assuming they were

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.326
they're misdemeanors

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:02.095
way beyond the statute of limitations.

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:03.663
So they have to cobble them together

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:04.931
to try and get a felony.

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:06.165
I'm going to speak to Michael

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.433
Cohen's attorney next.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.468
He says that

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:10.169
there is actual evidence

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.105
that your client, the former president,

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.640
participated, participated in falsifying

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.075
business records.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.710
Have you seen any such evidence

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.581
I know there's no such evidence.

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:22.448
I mean, look,

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:23.383
Michael Cohen's lawyer

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.884
spinning Michael Cohen side.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.853
Michael Cohen is a pathological convicted

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:27.186
liar.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:28.354
Perjury is like the banks,

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.722
the IRS, Congress,

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.157
now, we're saying you lied to the FEC

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:32.125
when they sent that letter saying

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:33.860
there was no campaign violation.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.561
I heard him on CNN the other day

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:36.062
saying that

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.530
when he pled guilty under oath,

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.432
when he became a new man,

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:40.433
he really wasn't guilty.

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:41.701
He was forced to plead guilty.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:42.802
So that's perjury.

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.771
If that's now true,

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:45.538
he's someone who was

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:47.006
constitutionally incapable

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.307
of telling the same story,

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.475
the same way twice.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:50.743
So I'm not really worried

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:51.711
about what Michael Cohen

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:52.378
is saying on this.

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.012
The records

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.248
and the facts will speak for themselves.

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:55.615
Okay.

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:56.115
I want to ask

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:57.183
about the judge

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.951
that we believe is going to preside

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.553
over the arraignment.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:01.287
The former president,

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:03.723
your client, was lashing out against him.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.559
His name is Juan Mershon. And

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.227
the former

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.263
president said that the judge hates him

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:12.498
and was handpicked by the D.A.

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.400
for this case for that reason.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.001
Are you going to ask

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:16.536
for a different judge

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.173
We are going to take the indictment,

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:22.341
evaluate all our legal options

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:25.011
and pursue everyone most vigorously.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:27.480
This is a case of political persecution.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.148
Had he not been running for office

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:29.949
right now

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:31.117
for the office of the presidency,

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:31.751
which, by the way,

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:32.652
the polls have shown

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:34.353
since this has been announced,

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:35.988
his numbers have gone up significantly.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:37.290
Had he not been running for presidency,

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.491
he would not have been indicted.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.626
Well, but let's talk about the area

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:41.794
where he'd been indicted.

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.396
My question is about the judge.

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:44.263
Will you ask.

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:47.033
Will you ask for a decision

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:47.700
Well,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.402
I just said we have to get the indictment

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:50.736
and then we will evaluate

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.905
every single legal maneuver.

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:53.139
You know,

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.140
I have no issue with this

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:54.907
judge whatsoever.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:55.975
Well, your client does.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:57.877
He says that his reputation.

00:07:57.877 --> 00:07:58.644
Well, what, Michael?

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.213
But my client has a right

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.147
to have an issue with everything.

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:02.648
He's been politically persecuted.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.150
Make no mistake about that, Dana.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.918
Whether you send the right or the left

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:06.819
or your supporter

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:08.354
or detractor of Donald Trump,

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:10.356
this should really bother you.

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:12.425
This this should really shake

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:14.126
the core of what we believe

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.328
our justice system should be about,

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.195
should not be weaponized.

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:17.230
To go after political opponents

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:17.597
